<title>SPAIN: Spain 1997 expenses seen at 18.1 trln ptas -Rato.</title>
<headline>Spain 1997 expenses seen at 18.1 trln ptas -Rato.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government's non-financial spending in 1997 will total 18.099 trillion pesetas, while non-financial income is seen totalling 16.09 trillion pesetas, Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Friday.</p>
<p>Speaking at a press conference after the cabinet approved the 1997 budget draft, Rato said this would bring the budget deficit to 2.0 trillion pesetas.</p>
<p>The cost of government debt would rise to 3.459 trillion pesetas in 1997, Rato added.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
